  "delivered": [
    "A caller-supplied GeneticCausalMatrix now invokes convert_genetic_matrix directly through an independent workbench. Existing cached-log genetic discovery remains separate; no source log, cached model or mined replacement matrix is required or read.",
    "All three original matrix vectors retain literal activity labels, vector order, duplicate members/partitions and even mismatched shapes until the native call. The returned normalized matrix remains a separate value: native conversion validates map lengths/indexes/nonempty partitions, sorts and deduplicates a copy, and preserves the original model before/after.",
    "Exactly one real native variant, TO_PETRI_NET(index0), is exposed with all three exact accepted aliases. The alternative raw signed int32 selector preserves unsupported indexes for native rejection. Named and indexed forms conflict by key presence; an explicitly supplied zero never hides a conflict.",
    "Complete conversion results include variant, normalized matrix, every public PetriNet field and signed int64 WorkflowMarkings. Raw source/sink storage and optional top-level transition names extend the established full net snapshot, preserving inactive values and engaged-empty metadata independently of derived aliases. Every arc occurrence, weight/reset/inhibitor vector, sparse discovery marking and structured name remains inspectable.",
    "Original bytes/SHA, transactional supplied-member presence, configured options, actual native calls and owned partial errors remain available. Independent original/source/normalized/result/PNML/legacy downloads, raw response/request/report, table CSV and selected-record JSON expose exact numeric/string state and preserve primary results independently of optional exports.",
    "The UI provides original matrix upload/text construction, the single native conversion, exact variant editors, ownership/cancellation and complete result inspection. Actual native API captures drive frontend replay/export tests; explicit omitted-control cases remain offline evidence where the browser builder submits its applicable defaults."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "This delivered feature does not establish full PM4Py parity or promote a strict unit. All86 packages,387 modules and228 incomplete strict units remain in scope.",
    "No new browser attempt was made under the unchanged saved-permission/managed-policy denial. The retained actual Feature63 attempt occurred after the user changed settings while Feature62/PID37476 listened at8562. Current coherent Feature64 native HTTP/API/production assets remain separate evidence; rendered layout, browser interaction and browser downloads remain unverified.",
    "The API accepts an original matrix rather than arbitrary supplied conversion results or host PetriNet objects. Converter-generated markings are signed native0/1 and its optional names/discovery metadata have their actual defaults. Arbitrary signed marking extremes, inactive metadata and optional legacy-export rejection are native codec test coverage, not invented injectable API controls.",
    "The equivalent inline aliases convert_genetic_matrix_to_petri_net and to_petri_net share the one canonical conversion surface; they do not create additional native variants. The native legacy JSON writer is a narrower optional artifact, while full result JSON and exact original bytes remain authoritative inspection/download carriers.",
    "Transport parser resource bounds remain separate from native semantic validation; no genetic-mining population/generation/activity limit is imposed on a supplied matrix. Client cancellation prevents stale result publication and does not stop an executing native call.",
    "The whole-catalogue inventory remains historical static availability evidence. Independent embedding filtering/full filtered EventLogs and keep_cases are next; weighted EMD languages, original object-centric playout, Table BOSE, independent original-source ILP/genetic discovery and all other recorded gaps and strict gates remain open.",
    "Failed or superseded preparation, build, API, export and frontend attempts remain retained and excluded from final successful counts."
  ],
